    "body": "## Motivation\n\n#36389 (merged 2026-09-25) added a required `global_num_tokens_cpu` parameter to `build_replay_fb_view` and updated the CUDA decode runner's call. `NPUGraphRunner.execute` builds the same view on its DFlash replay path (added in #37565 for MiMo-V2.5-Pro) and was not updated. Since #36389, replaying a captured graph with DFlash on Ascend fails before the graph runs:\n\n```\nTypeError: build_replay_fb_view() missing 1 required positional argument: 'global_num_tokens_cpu'\n```\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `NPUGraphRunner` subclasses `DecodeCudaGraphRunner`, so pass what the CUDA runner passes: `self._global_num_tokens_for_graph(...)` of the padded token count. That is the same helper the capture path uses. #36389 added this field to the replay view for LoRA with DP attention, and nothing under `hardware_backend/npu` reads it, so the NPU replay is unchanged apart from the TypeError going away.\n- No CPU or CUDA test reaches the Ascend replay, so I added `test/registered/unit/model_executor/runner/test_build_replay_fb_view_callers.py` (CPU suite), in the style of `test_plugin_hook_signatures.py`. It parses every `build_replay_fb_view(...)` call in `sglang.srt` and binds it to the function's signature. On `main` it fails at `npu_graph_runner.py:358` (`missing a required argument: 'global_num_tokens_cpu'`); with this PR both calls bind. If a parameter is added later and a caller is missed, the test will catch it on CPU.\n\n```\npython test/registered/unit/model_executor/runner/test_build_replay_fb_view_callers.py   # main: FAILED (errors=1), this PR: OK\npre-commit run --files <both files>                                                     # all hooks pass\n```\n\nI don't have Ascend hardware, so I could not run the DFlash replay end to end. The change only adds the missing argument.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\ncc @iridiumine (NPU DFlash, #37565) @erikwijmans (#36389)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
